      "date": "2026-07-23",
      "description": "National Gas Prices Jump to $4.09/gallon",
      "details": "The national average price for regular gasoline surged by 15 cents in one week, reaching $4.09 per gallon. This increase was attributed to rising crude oil prices and instability in the Strait of Hormuz. Higher gas prices typically reduce discretionary spending, leading to suppressed consumer confidence and reduced online purchases, especially for non-essential items like specialty food gifts.",
