      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "AAA"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "description": "Conference Board Consumer Confidence Declines in July",
      "details": "The Conference Board Consumer Confidence Index decreased by 1.4 points to 90.8 in July, down from 92.2 in June. The Present Situation Index also fell for the third consecutive month. A decline in consumer confidence, particularly when the Expectations Index remains below 80 (it was 74.7), signals economic pessimism. This typically leads to reduced discretionary spending and a cautious approach to gifting, negatively impacting ROAS and increasing CPA.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "The Conference Board"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-31",
      "description": "UofM Consumer Sentiment Rises to 55.2 in July",
      "details": "The University of Michigan Consumer Sentiment Index's final July reading rose to 55.2, an 11.5% increase from June, beating preliminary estimates. This improvement was largely driven by easing gas prices earlier in July. Increased consumer sentiment often correlates with a greater willingness to spend on discretionary items, potentially boosting ROAS and lowering CPA for a gifting brand.",
      "intensity": 2,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "boosts_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "low",
      "source": "University of Michigan"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-08-07",
      "description": "July US Jobs Report Shows Unexpected Payroll Decline",
      "details": "The U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics reported that total nonfarm payroll employment decreased by 23,000 in July, and the unemployment rate fell slightly to 4.1% as many people left the workforce. May and June payrolls were also revised significantly downwards. A weakening job market and revised negative employment figures can signal economic uncertainty, leading consumers to reduce non-essential spending, which would suppress ROAS and increase CPA.",
      "intensity": 3,
      "category": "wallet",
      "icon": "💰",
      "mood_impact": "suppresses_spending",
      "feed_dominance": "medium",
      "source": "U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-08-12",
